statement:
For every P ∈ ℕ there is a constant c₀ ≥ 0 with the following property. For every J ∈ ℕ, all points p_1, …, p_J ∈ ℝ^P and all radii σ_1, …, σ_J > 0, there is a function ζ : ℝ^P → ℝ such that:
- ζ is C^∞ (ContDiff ℝ ∞, i.e. ContDiff ℝ (⊤ : ℕ∞));
- 0 ≤ ζ(x) ≤ 1 for all x;
- ζ(x) = 0 for every x in an open ball B(p_j, σ_j);
- 1 − ζ(x) ≤ Σ_j 1_{B(p_j, 2σ_j)}(x) for all x;
- ‖Dζ(x)‖ ≤ Σ_j (c₀/σ_j)·1_{B(p_j, 2σ_j)}(x) for all x, where ‖Dζ(x)‖ is the operator norm of fderiv ℝ ζ x.
